// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 50 — Processes spawned at login
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Each line runs once when Niri starts. For daemons that support it,
// xdg-desktop-autostart (systemd) is an alternative.
//
// Tip: use spawn-sh-at-startup for shell pipelines or variable expansion.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── Shell ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Noctalia in daemon mode. Start it exactly once: if you also enable a systemd
// user unit for it you will get two shells fighting over the same D-Bus names.
spawn-at-startup "noctalia" "-d"

// Dropped with the Plasma theming: this rebuilt the KDE sycoca database, and
// kbuildsycoca6 comes from kservice, which is not installed.

// Clipboard history: wl-paste watches the clipboard and cliphist stores it.
// Type-specific watchers prevent duplicate entries (browsers offer both
// text/html and text/plain — without --type, cliphist stores both).
//
// NOTE: Noctalia keeps its own clipboard history (~/.local/state/noctalia/clipboard)
// and its panel (Mod+V) reads that, not cliphist. Keep these lines only if you
// still use cliphist from the terminal or other tools; otherwise delete them.
spawn-at-startup "bash" "-c" "wl-paste --type text --watch cliphist store &"
spawn-at-startup "bash" "-c" "wl-paste --type image --watch cliphist store &"

// ── Wallpaper ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// One tick of random-wallpaper's calendar rotation at login: the season when
// it begins, a holiday from a week before to a week after, the season again
// once that week is over.
//
// The systemd timer the app installs (random-wallpaper-auto.timer) does the
// same job while the session is up, and having both is deliberate, not sloppy —
// a tick only acts when today's period differs from the one it last applied,
// so the two cannot fight, and this line covers the seconds before the timer's
// first run. Nothing here looks at what wallpaper is currently set, so one you
// chose yourself survives every tick until the calendar moves on.
//
// Drop this line, or untick "Follow the calendar" in the app's Filters, to
// turn the rotation off; the setting is read by both callers.
spawn-at-startup "/usr/bin/random-wallpaper" "--auto"

// Polkit authentication agent — needed for GUI sudo prompts (software install,
// disk mount, etc.).
//
// NOTE: Noctalia has a built-in polkit panel (`noctalia msg panel-open polkit`).
// If it handles your prompts, this external agent is redundant — verify once on
// the new system (try a GUI action that needs root) and drop this line if so.
spawn-at-startup "/usr/lib/polkit-gnome/polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1"

// Dropped when moving off iNiR:
//   - inir.service (the Quickshell shell) — replaced by noctalia above
//   - awww-daemon (wallpaper) — Noctalia renders its own wallpaper surface
